For simplicity, let's define the interface with as few fields as possible. You can use a single interface for everything, even if some fields are rarely used:

```typescript
interface UserProfile {
  id: string;
  username: string;
  email: string;
  age?: number;
  hobbies?: string[];
  employment?: {
    jobTitle: string;
    company: string;
    location: string;
  };
}
```

This interface will be flexible enough to cover all possible user data, so you don't need to worry about tightly modeling your data structures.

